FlyWeb (156): adapted. 156 has no PageInfoBubbleTracker (it came with a
later 159 refactor); the bubble is tracked by the process-wide globals in
page_info_bubble_view_base.cc, which OnWidgetDestroying() clears and
CloseNow() reaches synchronously, so WebContentsDestroyed() only stops
observing and calls CloseNow(). The new browser test uses the 156 API
(GetShownBubbleType(), GetPageInfoBubbleForTesting() without arguments).
